<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Sant State</h1><p class="st-meta">1255 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Santrampur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Parmar Rajput state in eastern Gujarat, ruled from Santrampur, one of the states of the Rewa Kantha Agency.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The ruling family claimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parmar-rajputs">Parmar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> descent, and tradition dates the state to 1255. Little is reliably known about its early history.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Sant was a hilly, forested state with a large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhils">Bhil</a> population. In the colonial period it was part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rewa-kantha-agency">Rewa Kantha Agency</a> and paid tribute to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/baroda-state">Baroda State</a>. Its capital was the town of Santrampur.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Sant merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a> in 1948, and Santrampur is now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahisagar-district">Mahisagar district</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sant-state.jpg" alt="Sant State" width="320" height="487"><figcaption>Image: Ladabhai Parmar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joravarsinh,_ruler_of_Sunth_State_c._1922.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1255 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Santrampur</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Santrampur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1602&amp;focus=sant-state" aria-label="Sant State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6653 1322 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sant State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6973 1578L7364 1601M6973 1578L7364 1602M6973 1578L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6973 1578h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6973 1578h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1602&amp;focus=sant-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
